\subtree{
\title{3.1 tutorial/ — accept tests (94)}

\p{001–008 definitions, arrows, Π, λ, β (also under binders), binder domain needing whnf to be a sort; 013 theorem using a theorem; 015–027 universe arithmetic: \code{\verb~|imax 1 0~}, \code{\verb~|imax 0 1~}, \code{\verb~|imax 2 1~}, level parameters, \code{\verb~|imax u 0~}, \code{\verb~|imax u u~}, typing of Π via imax, \code{\verb~|max~} commutative/associative/idempotent/absorbing; 028–029 local variables, defeq of λs; 030–032 Church/Peano arithmetic by conversion; 033–035 \code{\verb~|let~} typing (dependent) and ζ; 036–045 inductive types: \code{\verb~|Empty~}, \code{\verb~|Bool~}, structures, \code{\verb~|And~}, \code{\verb~|Prod~}, \code{\verb~|PProd~}, \code{\verb~|PUnit~}, \code{\verb~|Eq~}, \code{\verb~|N~}, indexed \code{\verb~|RBTree~}; 055 constructor field types are reduced (whnf) when checking; 058–060 universe of fields (Prop may hold anything; \code{\verb~|Type u~} field in \code{\verb~|Type (u+1)~}); 062–072, 074 recursor \em{types} (Empty, Bool, structure, And, Prod, PProd, PUnit, Eq, N, RBTree, 2-constructor Prop → Prop-only elimination, \code{\verb~|Exists~}); 075 recursor of a one-constructor field-less type reduces on a variable major (structure eta on the major); 076–077 subsingleton elimination when data fields occur in the result type syntactically (and not after reduction); 078–082 ι-reduction (Bool, Prod, N, List, RBTree); 083–086 projection functions (\code{\verb~|And~}, \code{\verb~|Prod~}, \code{\verb~|PProd~}, \code{\verb~|PSigma~}); 089, 091 projections of proof fields out of a \code{\verb~|Prop~} structure before any dependent data field; 095 recursor of an indexed \code{\verb~|Prop~} family eliminating into \code{\verb~|Sort~}; 098 projection reduction; 099 rule K for \code{\verb~|Eq~}; 102–103 Nat literal typing and \code{\verb~|3 ≡ succ (succ (succ zero))~}; 104, 106, 107 proof irrelevance (also when the type only reduces to \code{\verb~|Prop~}, and between applications); 108–110 unit eta; 112 structure eta; 114–115 function eta; 119–122 reflexive inductives (positivity after reduction, recursor type, ι); 123–124 \code{\verb~|Acc.rec~} type and ι; 126–131 \code{\verb~|Quot~} signatures and reductions.}

\p{Three of them contain user axioms (034, 035, 107; and reject test 047): the con-leche family declines those.}
}

\subtree{
\title{3.2 tutorial/ — reject tests (47)}

\table{
\tr{\th{test}\th{why it is invalid}\th{check that catches it (official 4.36.0 message)}}
\tr{\td{002_badDef}\td{\code{\verb~|def badDef : Prop := Type~}}\td{value type vs declared type ("declaration type mismatch … has type Type 1 … expected Prop")}}
\tr{\td{009_forallSortBad}\td{Π whose third binder domain is a proof variable}\td{domain's type must whnf to a sort ("type expected x")}}
\tr{\td{010_nonTypeType}\td{definition whose "type" is the function \code{\verb~|constType~}}\td{declared type must be a type ("type expected constType")}}
\tr{\td{011_nonTypeAxiom}\td{same for an axiom}\td{axioms need the same check}}
\tr{\td{012_nonPropThm}\td{theorem whose statement \code{\verb~|Prop~} has sort \code{\verb~|Type~}}\td{theorem type must be a proposition ("type of theorem … is not a proposition")}}
\tr{\td{014_selfProof}\td{theorem's value is the theorem itself}\td{constant not in the environment while being checked ("unknown constant")}}
\tr{\td{019_tut06_bad01}\td{\code{\verb~|levelParams = [u, u]~}}\td{duplicate universe parameter}}
\tr{\td{046_inductBadNonSort}\td{inductive whose type is a λ}\td{"type expected"}}
\tr{\td{047_inductBadNonSort2}\td{inductive whose type is the axiom \code{\verb~|aType : Type~}}\td{type must end in a \code{\verb~|Sort~} ("type expected aType")}}
\tr{\td{048_inductLevelParam}\td{inductive with \code{\verb~|[u, u]~}}\td{duplicate universe parameter}}
\tr{\td{049_inductTooFewParams}\td{\code{\verb~|numParams = 2~}, type has one binder}\td{"incorrect number of parameters"}}
\tr{\td{050_inductWrongCtorParams}\td{constructor parameter of type \code{\verb~|Type~} where the inductive's is \code{\verb~|Prop~}; result \code{\verb~|I aProp~}}\td{constructor telescope must start with the block's parameters and return \code{\verb~|I params…~} ("invalid occurrence of datatype … must be applied to the parameters and universe levels")}}
\tr{\td{051_inductWrongCtorResParams}\td{result \code{\verb~|I y x~} (parameters swapped)}\td{same}}
\tr{\td{052_inductWrongCtorResLevel}\td{result \code{\verb~|I.{u2,u1} x y~}}\td{same (universe arguments must be the declared ones in order)}}
\tr{\td{053_inductInIndex}\td{result \code{\verb~|I (I aProp)~}: the type inside an index}\td{"invalid return type"}}
\tr{\td{054_indNeg}\td{\code{\verb~|mk : (I → I) → I~}}\td{strict positivity ("non positive occurrence")}}
\tr{\td{056_reduceCtorType.mk}\td{constructor type \code{\verb~|id Type I~} (not a manifest Π/application)}\td{constructor type as a whole is \em{not} reduced ("invalid return type")}}
\tr{\td{057_indNegReducible}\td{field \code{\verb~|(constType aType I → I)~}; the occurrence would vanish by reducing inside the domain}\td{only whnf of the field type; inner occurrence is negative}}
\tr{\td{061_typeWithTooHighTypeField.mk}\td{\code{\verb~|T : Type~} with a field \code{\verb~|Type~}}\td{field universe ≤ inductive universe ("universe level … is too big")}}
\tr{\td{073_BogusRecursor}\td{recursor record claims type \code{\verb~|False~}, used to prove \code{\verb~|False~}}\td{regenerate recursors ("incorrect number of universe levels parameters for 'BogusRecursor.rec', \verb~|#~1 expected, \verb~|#~0 provided")}}
\tr{\td{087_projOutOfRange}\td{\code{\verb~|z.3~} on \code{\verb~|And~}}\td{field index range ("invalid projection")}}
\tr{\td{088_projNotStruct}\td{projection out of \code{\verb~|N~} (two constructors)}\td{structure-likeness ("invalid projection")}}
\tr{\td{090, 092_projProp2/4}\td{data field out of a \code{\verb~|Prop~} structure}\td{projected field of a proposition must be a proof}}
\tr{\td{093_projProp5}\td{proof field whose type depends on an earlier data field}\td{walking past a data field that later fields depend on is forbidden}}
\tr{\td{094_projProp6}\td{proof field located after such a dependent data field}\td{same}}
\tr{\td{096, 097_projIndexData(2)}\td{\code{\verb~|x.[PropStructure#i]~} where \code{\verb~|x : ProjDataIndex n~} (and the intended point: data stored in a \code{\verb~|Prop~} family)}\td{projection's type name must be the head of the struct's type; Prop rule ("invalid projection")}}
\tr{\td{100_ruleKbad}\td{\code{\verb~|Eq.rec a (h : true = false) = a~} by \code{\verb~|rfl~}}\td{K only when the major's type matches the constructor's ("declaration type mismatch")}}
\tr{\td{101_ruleKAcc}\td{\code{\verb~|Acc.rec … h = a~} by \code{\verb~|rfl~}}\td{\code{\verb~|Acc~} is not K-like (its constructor has fields)}}
\tr{\td{105_proofIrrelevanceBad}\td{\code{\verb~|h1 = h2~} for \code{\verb~|h1 h2 : p~}, \code{\verb~|p : Type~}}\td{proof irrelevance only in \code{\verb~|Prop~}}}
\tr{\td{111_indexedUnitEta}\td{\code{\verb~|x = y~} for \code{\verb~|x y : IndexedUnit true~}}\td{unit-like eta not for indexed families}}
\tr{\td{113_indexedStructEta}\td{\code{\verb~|IndexedSingleton.mk True.intro = x~}}\td{structure eta not for indexed families}}
\tr{\td{116_funEtaBad}\td{\code{\verb~|(fun x => f (g x)) = f~}}\td{eta must compare bodies}}
\tr{\td{117_reflOccLeft}\td{field \code{\verb~|Nat → (I → Nat)~}}\td{positivity behind arrows}}
\tr{\td{118_reflOccInIndex}\td{field \code{\verb~|Nat → I (I α)~}; as exported the constructor type is also ill-typed}\td{positivity / type check of the constructor ("application type mismatch")}}
\tr{\td{125_accRecNoEta}\td{\code{\verb~|Acc.rec … (h : Acc r a) = p~} by \code{\verb~|rfl~}}\td{no structure eta for \code{\verb~|Acc~} majors}}
\tr{\td{132_dup_defs}\td{two definitions named \code{\verb~|dup_defs~}}\td{duplicate constant name ("Duplicate declaration", raised by the reader)}}
\tr{\td{133_dup_ind_def}\td{definition named like an inductive type}\td{same}}
\tr{\td{134_dup_ctor_def}\td{definition named like a constructor}\td{same}}
\tr{\td{135_dup_rec_def}\td{definition named like a recursor}\td{same}}
\tr{\td{136_misnamed_rec_user}\td{recursor exported as \code{\verb~|misnamed_rec.not_rec~}, used by a definition}\td{recursors are generated, named \code{\verb~|<type>.rec~} ("unknown constant 'misnamed_rec.not_rec'")}}
\tr{\td{137_dup_rec_def2}\td{misnamed recursor and a definition taking \code{\verb~|dup_rec_def2.rec~}}\td{generated name collides ("constant has already been declared")}}
\tr{\td{138_dup_ctor_rec}\td{constructor named \code{\verb~|X.rec~}}\td{duplicate name}}
\tr{\td{139_DupConCon}\td{two constructors with one name}\td{duplicate name}}
\tr{\td{140_falseFromUnsafe}\td{theorem \code{\verb~|False := unsafeLoop~} (\code{\verb~|safety: unsafe~})}\td{unsafe constants are not visible to safe ones ("unknown constant 'unsafeLoop'")}}
\tr{\td{141_falseFromPartial}\td{theorem \code{\verb~|False := partialLoop~} (\code{\verb~|safety: partial~})}\td{same for partial}}
}

\p{Top-checker policy on 140/141: nano-lean, gruszka, rpylean, pestka, kefir, palladium, nanoda, nanobruijn, tenet-jvm, official reject; sokonanoda and the con-leche family decline (allowed, but one more decline).}
}

